  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nFor late Saturday night into Sunday and possibly Monday, mid and\nhigh level moisture from tropical cyclones Odalys and Polo will\nspread into the area from the southwest and south. Sunday will be\nmostly cloudy with a chance of showers. A low pressure system\nmoving inland through California is expected to bring drying from\nthe northwest some time Monday into Tuesday.\n\nHigh temperatures on Sunday will be 5 to 10 degrees cooler and\nanother few to 5 degrees cooler for Monday with Monday high\ntemperatures near average near the coast and around 5 degrees\nbelow average for inland areas. High temperatures on Monday will\nrange from the 70s near the coast to the lower to mid 80s for the\nInland Empire with the lower deserts in the lower 90s.\n\nHigh pressure aloft is expected to bring warming for Tuesday and\nWednesday. If east to northeast winds develop, there could be\nadditional warming for the coast and valleys on those days.",
